    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "dc:source": "act.pdf, p.173",
      "skos:note": "Inducing a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing a rebate, commission, or other benefit in return for assisting others is prohibited.",
      "skos:prefLabel": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "167(1) Referral selling"
      },
      "wasDerivedFrom": "act.pdf",
      "asserts": [
        "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-norm",
        "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
        "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2",
        "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-ltl-3",
        "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-diffusion-4",
        "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-cogai-5"
      ],
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:integrityHash": "d6e42d78d46be60cef8984f444a40ed2b2545275de57b3003307423e8c447d2d",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "realizedBy": "doc:act#sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1",
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "partOf": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(b) the receipt of the rebate, commission or other benefit is contingent on an event occurring after that contract is made.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal containment of induced consumer acquisition.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal Containment",
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, induces a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing that the consumer will, after the contract for the acquisition of the goods or services is made, receive a rebate, commission or other benefit in return for:  (i) giving the person the names of prospective customers; or  (ii) otherwise assisting the person to supply goods or services to other consumers; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(b) the receipt of the rebate, commission or other benefit is contingent on an event occurring after that contract is made.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Knowledge representation of induced consumer acquisition.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Knowledge Representation",
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, induces a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing that the consumer will, after the contract for the acquisition of the goods or services is made, receive a rebate, commission or other benefit in return for:  (i) giving the person the names of prospective customers; or  (ii) otherwise assisting the person to supply goods or services to other consumers; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of inducing a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing a rebate, commission, or other benefit in return for assisting others.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, induces a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing that the consumer will, after the contract for the acquisition of the goods or services is made, receive a rebate, commission or other benefit in return for:  (i) giving the person the names of prospective customers; or  (ii) otherwise assisting the person to supply goods or services to other consumers; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(b) the receipt of the rebate, commission or other benefit is contingent on an event occurring after that contract is made.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Information spread of induced consumer acquisition.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Information Spread",
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, induces a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing that the consumer will, after the contract for the acquisition of the goods or services is made, receive a rebate, commission or other benefit in return for:  (i) giving the person the names of prospective customers; or  (ii) otherwise assisting the person to supply goods or services to other consumers; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(b) the receipt of the rebate, commission or other benefit is contingent on an event occurring after that contract is made.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recurring trace of induced consumer acquisition.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurring Trace",
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, induces a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing that the consumer will, after the contract for the acquisition of the goods or services is made, receive a rebate, commission or other benefit in return for:  (i) giving the person the names of prospective customers; or  (ii) otherwise assisting the person to supply goods or services to other consumers; and"
    },
